      "writtenOn": "2025-05-27T18:21:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You should be able to to change `pwr-sys-rst-l` from `intel,ap-pwrseq-external` to `intel,ap-pwrseq-gpio`?\n\n`intel,ap-pwrseq-external` is meant to be used when the corresponding power signal needs additional handling beyond reading or writing a single GPIO.  The platform then needs to create the routines `board_power_signal_set` and `board_power_signal_get`.\n\nGPIOs connected to an I/O expander can be handled directly by `intel,ap-pwrseq-gpio`, just like GPIOs connected directly to the EC.",
      "parentUuid": "cf62c504_ad950b45",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 28,
        "startChar": 0,
